---
title: Types
description: Public TypeScript types, inference rules, channels, definitions, scenes, hosts, focus, rendering, and custom extension contracts.
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Charts is inference-first. A mark's source data and channel selectors\nflow through its definition into scales, axis formatters, host and adapter\ncallbacks, focus callbacks, and selection callbacks. Normal application code\nshould not cast chart definitions or supply adapter generics."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Browser applications can import types from the package root. Platform-neutral\nlibraries can import the same definition, mark, scene, runtime, focus, and\ntooltip-model contracts from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/types"},{"type":"text","value":"; DOM host and renderer\ntypes remain available from the root."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/types/core"},{"type":"text","value":" entry exposes the module that declares the\ncore types. TypeScript uses this entry when emitting inferred declarations\nfor exported marks and chart definitions. You do not need to annotate those\nexports or import package-internal files."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This entry also exposes the supporting inference and extension contracts:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Purpose"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartSpecBase"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shared guide, color, resource, and layout options"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StoredChartSpec"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stored marks and scale registry used by definition inference"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CheckedChartSpec"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Checks a stored spec against its marks' scale requirements"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MarkScaleBindings"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional named x and y scale bindings"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MarkChannelOutput"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inferred channel output with a widened fallback"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MarkCallOptions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Combines inferred selectors with non-inferred options"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DecorativeChartMark"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Marks geometry as decorative while retaining its source types"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartLegendPlacement"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Top or bottom placement for a color legend"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartHostControl"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scene descriptor for an optional host control"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartHostControlExtensionToken"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renderer-neutral identity and factory for a host control"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"callback-shape","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Callback shape"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Public callbacks take at most two arguments: primary data or purpose first,\nthen a named context or options object. A callback without a distinct primary\npayload takes one context object. Standard comparators, exact upstream\nprotocols, paired geometry, and consumer-called service methods are explicit\nexceptions."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"values-and-channels","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Values and channels"}]},{"type":"code","value":"type ChartValue = number | string | Date\ntype ChartKey = string | number\n\ninterface ChannelAccessorContext<TDatum> {\n  index: number\n  data: readonly TDatum[]\n}\n\ntype ChannelAccessor<TDatum, TValue> = (\n  datum: TDatum,\n  context: ChannelAccessorContext<TDatum>,\n) => TValue\n\ntype Channel<TDatum, TValue> =\n  ChannelField<TDatum, TValue> | ChannelAccessor<TDatum, TValue>\n\ntype VisualChannel<TDatum, TValue> = TValue | ChannelAccessor<TDatum, TValue>","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The corresponding public type names are "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChannelAccessor"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChannelAccessorContext"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VisualChannel"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts only datum keys whose declared values are compatible with\nthe channel, or an accessor that derives a value from the row. Its context\ncontains the index and full readonly data array. A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VisualChannel"},{"type":"text","value":" replaces\nthe field-name form with a constant: it accepts either one constant value or\nan accessor."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { lineY } from '@tanstack/charts'\n\ninterface Row {\n  date: Date\n  value: number\n  label: string\n  series: 'actual' | 'forecast'\n}\n\nlineY(rows, {\n  x: 'date', // Date\n  y: 'value', // number\n  z: 'series',\n  stroke: (row) => (row.series === 'actual' ? '#2563eb' : '#60a5fa'),\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChannelField"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChannelOutput"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OptionChannelOutput"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"WidenChartValue"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartAxisValue"},{"type":"text","value":" are exported for extension authors.\nLiteral chart values widen to their semantic primitive so a literal row does\nnot produce an unusably narrow scale or callback type."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"inference-path","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inference path"}]},{"type":"code","value":"source datum\n  → mark channel outputs\n  → ChartMark point and scale value types\n  → ChartSpec scale registry and definition datum/x/y unions\n  → scale and formatter types\n  → host and adapter callback types","lang":"text"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Marks in one chart may have different datum types. The definition exposes their\nunion. TypeScript narrowing is therefore required when a callback handles\nheterogeneous layers."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMarkScaleX"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMarkScaleY"},{"type":"text","value":" control the value types accepted by the\nreserved scale entries. Canonical definitions always include "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scales.x"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scales.y"},{"type":"text","value":"; use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" when a dimension is unused. A mark bound to another\nscale ID does not widen the reserved entry's value type."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rect and custom interval marks can distinguish materialized scale values from\ninteraction point values. The exported extractors are:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMarkDatum"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartSpecDatum"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartSpecXValue"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartSpecYValue"},{"type":"text","value":"\nare available from the root entry point. The four "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMarkPoint*"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMarkScale*"},{"type":"text","value":" extractors below come from the exceptional\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/mark/scale-values"},{"type":"text","value":" subpath."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Extracts"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMarkDatum<TMark>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Original datum"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMarkPointX<TMark>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interaction x value; exported from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/mark/scale-values"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMarkPointY<TMark>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interaction y value; exported from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/mark/scale-values"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMarkScaleX<TMark>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All x values materialized for scale typing; exported from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/mark/scale-values"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMarkScaleY<TMark>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All y values materialized for scale typing; exported from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/mark/scale-values"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartSpecDatum<TSpec>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Datum union across marks"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartSpecXValue<TSpec>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interaction x union across marks"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartSpecYValue<TSpec>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interaction y union across marks"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stateful mark presentation uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMarkStateContext"},{"type":"text","value":" as one object bag for\nthe datum, index, data, point, focus, pointer, and matching helper. A\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMarkStateSelector"},{"type":"text","value":" handles the common declarative cases, while callbacks\ncan return any "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMarkStateValue"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMarkStateStyle"},{"type":"text","value":" is the complete\nstyle vocabulary; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartDotStateStyle"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartBarStateStyle"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartRectStateStyle"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartLineStateStyle"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartAreaStateStyle"},{"type":"text","value":", and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartTextStateStyle"},{"type":"text","value":" narrow it to properties each mark can render. All six\naccept "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeDasharray"},{"type":"text","value":" for a state-driven dash pattern."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"definitions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Definitions"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Purpose"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartSpec"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Marks plus a positional scale registry, guides, color, resources, and layout"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StaticChartDefinition"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A directly compilable spec with inferred datum and semantic x/y phantom types"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ResponsiveChartDefinition"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Responsive chart builder"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartDefinition"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Static or responsive union"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartDefinitionForTooltipHost"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Definition restricted to one tooltip host brand"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DomChartDefinition"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Definition compatible with the DOM tooltip host"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ComposableStaticChartDefinition"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Static definition safe to embed in a composed view"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ComposableResponsiveChartDefinition"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Responsive definition safe to embed in a composed view"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ComposableChartDefinition"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Static or responsive composable definition"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartBuildContext"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Current size and platform-default build-time theme"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The complete overloads and runtime rules are in\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./chart-definitions.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chart Definition API"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"marks-and-scenes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Marks and scenes"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Purpose"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMark"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Public initialized-mark factory plus inferred point, scale value, and scale ID types"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMarkOptions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shared optional mark renderer contract"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMarkRenderer"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Universal renderer-selection token stored on mark-owned scene nodes"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CartesianChartMark"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cartesian mark alias that derives selected x and y scale IDs from its options"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RectCornerRadii"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Physical top-left, top-right, bottom-right, and bottom-left radius tuple"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RectRadius"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Uniform numeric radius or physical per-corner tuple"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"BarEndRadius"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Semantic bar-end radius with optional outer-stack or per-segment behavior"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"BarRadius"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Uniform, physical, accessor, or semantic bar-end radius"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OptionScaleId"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resolves an optional named-scale selector to its fallback scale ID"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MarkInitializeContext"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mark layer index"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InitializedMark"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable ID, channels, viewport ownership, render, and optional resolved layout"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MarkInitialization"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Direct-render or resolved-layout initializer result"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ResolvedLayoutMarkInitialization"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Layout initializer before "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createMark"},{"type":"text","value":" normalization"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MaterializedChannel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Values contributed to an optional named scale"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MarkRenderContext"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Final chart bounds, scales, theme, color resolver, and layout"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MarkResolvedLayoutContext"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Final positional scales and bounds for pure mark-local layout"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"ty